    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/10–446</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">SWN–4800</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-04">4 October 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Delivery of Reparations Goods in Japan</p>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>References:</cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. SWNCC 236/20</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>. SWNCC 236/25</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>. SWNCC 236/27</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>Enclosed herewith is a copy of SWNCC 236/27, a revision of reference <hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi> as amended by reference <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi> and approved by the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee on 3
                    October 1946.</p>
                <p>It is requested that the statement of the U.S. position in the Appendix be
                    forwarded by the State Department to the U.S. Member of the Far Eastern
                        Commission.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d428-f1"/></p>
                <closer>For the State–War–Navy Coordinating Committee:<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Ernest</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Gross</hi></signed><lb/>for <signed>J. H. Hilldring</signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d428-a1.xml" xpointer="d428-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d428-f1" n="22" xml:id="d428-f1-content">
                <p>This was clone October 11, with a view to obtaining a policy decision on the
                    subject.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
